# TextFSM template: Nokia SR OS / TiMOS
# `show router … bgp routes … hunt|detail`. Shared by bgp.route /
# bgp.community / bgp.largecommunity / bgp.aspath because all four
# queries emit the same RIB-In/RIB-Out path-block shape.
#
# Canonical RIB-In block (truncated):
#   ===============================================================================
#   BGP Router ID:10.0.0.1        AS:65000       Local AS:65000
#   ===============================================================================
#   Legend -
#   Status codes  : u - used, s - suppressed, h - history, d - decayed, * - valid
#                   l - leaked, x - stale, > - best, b - backup, p - purge
#   ===============================================================================
#   BGP RIB-In Entries
#   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Network        : 1.1.1.0/24
#   Nexthop        : 10.0.0.2
#   From           : 10.0.0.2
#   Res. Nexthop   : 10.0.0.2
#   Local Pref.    : 100                    Interface Name : to-peer
#   Aggregator AS  : None                   Aggregator     : None
#   Atomic Aggr.   : Not Atomic             MED            : 0
#   AIGP Metric    : None
#   Connector      :
#   Community      : 65000:100 65000:200
#   Large Community: 214503:8:3607
#   Cluster        : No Cluster Members
#   Originator Id  : None                   Peer Router Id : 10.0.0.2
#   IPv4 Label     : N/A
#   Flags          : Used Valid Best IGP
#   Route Source   : External
#   AS-Path        : 65001 65002
#   Peer AS        : 65001
#   Age            : 1d02h00m00s
#   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Capture strategy:
#   - The Filldown'd `prefix` carries the Network field across the
#     multi-line block. Record fires on the `Age` line which is the
#     last per-path field we care about (everything below it is
#     operator-pref noise).
#   - `communities`, `large_communities`, and `as_path` are captured
#     as single tokens spanning the whole value list. The
#     projector's splitListToken() expands them per-entry.
#   - `best` is detected by a substring presence of the literal
#     `Best` keyword in the Flags line; the dedicated Value avoids
#     greedy `${flags}` capture eating it.
Value Filldown router_id ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value Filldown local_asn (\d+)
Value Required prefix ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+/\d+)
Value nexthop ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_asn (\d+)
Value local_pref (\d+)
Value med (\d+)
Value communities (\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+)*)
Value large_communities (\d+:\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+:\d+)*)
Value best (Best)
Value as_path (\d+(?:\s+\d+)*)
Value age (\S+)

Start
  ^BGP\s+Router\s+ID:${router_id}\s+AS:${local_asn}
  ^BGP\s+RIB-In\s+Entries -> Routes
  ^BGP\s+RIB-Out\s+Entries -> Routes
  ^Network\s*:\s+${prefix} -> Routes

Routes
  ^Network\s*:\s+${prefix}
  ^Nexthop\s*:\s+${nexthop}
  ^From\s*:\s+${peer_ip}
  ^Local\s+Pref\.\s*:\s+${local_pref}
  ^Atomic\s+Aggr\..*MED\s*:\s+${med}
  ^Community\s*:\s+${communities}\s*$$
  ^Large\s+Community:\s+${large_communities}\s*$$
  # Flags line: presence of literal `Best` substring marks active.
  ^Flags\s*:\s+[^\n]*?${best}
  ^Flags\s*:\s+
  ^AS-Path\s*:\s+${as_path}\s*$$
  ^Peer\s+AS\s*:\s+${peer_asn}
  ^Age\s*:\s+${age} -> Record
  ^-+\s*$$
